License compatibility with KeyPrism (MIT)
-----------------------------------------
All runtime dependencies above are permissive (MIT / BSD / Apache-2.0 /
ISC). Known obligations to track (none blocking internal use):
  - LGPL-2.1 (libsndfile via soundfile, FFmpeg libs via PyAV wheels):
    keep them unmodified as separately-linked libraries and carry the
    LGPL notices in any binary distribution. TODO(3.10).
  - Apache-2.0 (basic-pitch, huggingface-hub, tensorflow): requires
    retaining NOTICE files and stating changes if modified. Compatible
    with MIT distribution; no action beyond this inventory.
  - Research-only datasets/weights (MUSDB18-HQ lineage of htdemucs):
    usage restriction travels with the weights, not with KeyPrism
    code; documented above. TODO(3.10) as noted.
